From: CARGT <engineering@cargt.com>
Subject: [PATCH] init-resize: fsck the rootfs partition before growing it

Every other filesystem resized here (userfs, vendorfs, bootfs) is
force-checked with e2fsck before resize2fs grows it. The rootfs case
was missing that check, so resize2fs ran against an unverified
filesystem on first boot. This produced severe ext4 metadata
corruption on affected units (garbage i_size/i_blocks, impossible
timestamps, orphaned inodes reported by a later e2fsck run) -- match
the same fsck-then-resize pattern used for the other three partitions.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not sent upstream to ST]

--- a/init-resize.sh
+++ b/init-resize.sh
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
                                     ;;
                                 root*)
                                     echo "RESIZE ROOTFS [$DEVICE]"
-                                    /sbin/resize2fs $DEVICE
+                                    /sbin/e2fsck -f -y -c -C 0 $DEVICE && /sbin/resize2fs $DEVICE
                                     ;;
                                 vendor*)
                                     echo "RESIZE VENDORFS [$DEVICE]"
